/-!
# Compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms

Let `σ` be a two-form on a manifold `M` and `φ_t`, `t ∈ [0, 1]`, a smooth diffeotopy of `M`. In
McDuff–Salamon, §3.1, `φ_t` is a compactly supported Hamiltonian isotopy when every `φ_t`
preserves `σ` and `φ_t` is generated by a time-dependent Hamiltonian `H_t` that vanishes, for
every `t`, outside one compact set `K ⊆ M`. Tau Ceti reads Hamiltonians along the motion, as
`F (x, t) = H_t (φ_t x)` (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian`), so the condition becomes
`F (x, t) = 0` whenever `φ_t x ∉ K`
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian`); read on `M` with
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy`, it is the original condition
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff_isGeneratedBy`). The final maps of
these diffeotopies form the group `Ham_c(M, σ)`
(`TauCeti.SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ Φ`: `Φ` is a Hamiltonian diffeotopy of
  `σ` with a Hamiltonian that vanishes off a compact set.
* `TauCeti.SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ`: the group `Ham_c(M, σ)` of final
  maps of such diffeotopies.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff_isGeneratedBy`: the predicate holds
  exactly when every `φ_t` preserves `σ` and `φ_t` is generated by a function on `M × [0, 1]`
  that vanishes off a compact subset of `M`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.trans`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.symm`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph`: composites, inverses and
  conjugates by diffeomorphisms preserving `σ` of compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopies are
  compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopies.
* `TauCeti.SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_le_hamiltonianGroup`: `Ham_c(M, σ)` lies
  in `Ham(M, σ)`.
* `TauCeti.SmoothForm.normal_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_diffeomorphStabilizer`:
  `Ham_c(M, σ)` is normal in the group of diffeomorphisms preserving `σ`.
* `TauCeti.SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_eq_hamiltonianGroup`: on a compact
  manifold, `Ham_c(M, σ) = Ham(M, σ)`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian`: for a symplectic `σ`, every smooth
  function on `M × [0, 1]` that vanishes off a compact set `K ⊆ M` generates a compactly
  supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy, which fixes every point outside `K`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_interior_velocity_eq`: for a symplectic `σ`, a smooth family of closed
  one-forms `Ω_t` vanishing off a compact set `L` is `ι_{X_t} σ` for the velocity `X_t` of a
  diffeotopy that preserves `σ` and fixes every point outside `L`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_interior_velocity_eq_add_mextDeriv`: the case `Ω_t = β_t + dG_t`, for
  closed `β_t` vanishing off `L` and a smooth `G` vanishing off `C`, with fixed set `L ∪ C`.
* `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.isHamiltonian_iff_and_normal_hamiltonianGroup`: the
  characterizations of Hamiltonian diffeotopies, uniqueness of their generating functions, the
  rules for composites, inverses and conjugates, and the normality of `Ham(M, σ)` and
  `Ham_c(M, σ)` in the group of diffeomorphisms preserving `σ`, together.

## Implementation notes

The predicate asks for vanishing off a compact set rather than for a compact support of `H_t`, so
that `M` need not be Hausdorff; on a Hausdorff `M` the two agree. It is not the condition that the
diffeotopy fixes every point off a compact set: adding to a Hamiltonian a function of `t` alone,
on each connected component, gives another Hamiltonian of the same diffeotopy
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.exists_sub_eq`), and a diffeotopy can be compactly supported
without having a Hamiltonian that vanishes off a compact set.

The subgroup and its API follow Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup`,
`TauCeti.SmoothForm.mul_mul_inv_mem_hamiltonianGroup` and
`TauCeti.SmoothForm.normal_hamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_diffeomorphStabilizer`, and the rules for
the predicate add compact sets to Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.trans`,
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.symm` and `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph`.

The diffeotopy of `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_interior_velocity_eq` is Tau Ceti's
`TauCeti.timeDependentFlowDiffeotopy` of the fields `(σ♭)⁻¹ α_u`, `α` being the extension
`TauCeti.SmoothForm.timeExtend` of `Ω` to `ℝ × M`, by Seeley's operator. The extension still
vanishes off `L` (`SymplecticGeometry.timeExtend_eq_zero`), so the fields vanish off `L` and their
suspension is complete (`TauCeti.isCompleteVectorField_timeDependentSuspensionField`). Its slices
preserve `σ` because the `Ω_t` are closed for `t ∈ [0, 1]`
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.forall_timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer_iff`); past the ends of `[0, 1]`
the extended forms need not be closed, and they are not needed there.
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_interior_velocity_eq_add_mextDeriv` applies it to `Ω = β + dG`, whose
slices are `β_t + dG_t`, and `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian` is its
case `β = 0`: the equation
`ι_{X_t} σ = dG_t` says that `X_t` is the Hamiltonian vector field of `G_t`, so `G` generates the
diffeotopy.

## References

* [D. McDuff and D. Salamon, *Introduction to Symplectic Topology*][McDuffSalamon2017], §3.1,
  Definition 3.1.13, Exercise 3.1.14 and Remark 3.1.15.
* R. T. Seeley, *Extension of $C^\infty$ functions defined in a half space*,
  Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 15 (1964), 625–626.
-/

public noncomputable section

open Set
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace TauCeti

namespace Diffeotopy

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]
  [IsManifold J ∞ M] {σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2} {Φ Ψ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M}

/-- A diffeotopy `φ_t` is a **compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy** of the two-form `σ`
when every `φ_t` preserves `σ` and `φ_t` has a Hamiltonian `F`, read along the motion, with
`F (x, t) = 0` whenever `φ_t x` lies outside a fixed compact set `K`. Equivalently, `φ_t` is
generated by a time-dependent Hamiltonian `H_t = F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` that vanishes off `K` for every
`t` (`isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff_isGeneratedBy`). -/
def IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian (σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2) (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) : Prop :=
  (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧
    ∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F ∧ ∃ K : Set M, IsCompact K ∧ ∀ p, Φ.cylinderMap p ∉ K → F p = 0

/-- Unfolding `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian`. -/
theorem isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ↔
    (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧
      ∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F ∧ ∃ K : Set M, IsCompact K ∧
        ∀ p, Φ.cylinderMap p ∉ K → F p = 0 :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **The reading on `M`.** A diffeotopy `φ_t` is a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy of
`σ` exactly when every `φ_t` preserves `σ` and `φ_t` is generated by a function `G` on
`M × [0, 1]` (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy`) with `G (x, t) = 0` whenever `x` lies outside
a fixed compact set `K`. -/
theorem isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff_isGeneratedBy : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ↔
    (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧
      ∃ G, Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G ∧ ∃ K : Set M, IsCompact K ∧
        ∀ p : M × unitInterval, p.1 ∉ K → G p = 0 := by
  refine and_congr_right fun _ ↦ ⟨fun ⟨F, hF, K, hK, hFK⟩ ↦ ⟨_, hF.isGeneratedBy, K, hK,
    fun p hp ↦ hFK _ ?_⟩, fun ⟨G, hG, K, hK, hGK⟩ ↦ ⟨_, hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.2 hG, K, hK,
    fun _ hp ↦ hGK _ hp⟩⟩
  rwa [cylinderMap_apply, apply_mk_symm_apply]

/-- A compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy is Hamiltonian. -/
theorem IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.isHamiltonian (hΦ : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ) :
    Φ.IsHamiltonian σ :=
  isHamiltonian_iff.2 ⟨hΦ.1, hΦ.2.choose, hΦ.2.choose_spec.1⟩

/-- The constant diffeotopy is a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy, with the zero
Hamiltonian and the empty compact set. -/
theorem isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_refl :
    (refl J ∞ M).IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ :=
  ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_refl_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer, 0, hasHamiltonian_refl, ∅,
    isCompact_empty, fun _ _ ↦ rfl⟩

/-- The pointwise composite `ψ_t ∘ φ_t` of compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopies is a
compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy. If the Hamiltonians of `φ_t` and `ψ_t` vanish off
`K_φ` and `K_ψ`, that of the composite vanishes off `K_ψ ∪ ⋃_t ψ_t (K_φ)`. -/
theorem IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.trans (hΦ : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ)
    (hΨ : Ψ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ) : (Φ.trans Ψ).IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF, KΦ, hKΦ, hFK⟩ := hΦ
  obtain ⟨hΨσ, G, hG, KΨ, hKΨ, hGK⟩ := hΨ
  refine ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_trans_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hΦσ hΨσ, _, hF.trans hG hΨσ,
    KΨ ∪ Ψ.cylinderMap '' (KΦ ×ˢ univ),
    hKΨ.union ((hKΦ.prod isCompact_univ).image Ψ.contMDiff_cylinderMap.continuous),
    fun p hp ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [cylinderMap_trans, Function.comp_apply, mem_union, not_or] at hp
  rw [hGK _ hp.1, hFK p fun h ↦ hp.2 ⟨_, ⟨h, mem_univ _⟩, rfl⟩, add_zero]

/-- The pointwise inverse `φ_t⁻¹` of a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy is a compactly
supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy. If the Hamiltonian of `φ_t` vanishes off `K`, that of the
inverse vanishes off `⋃_t φ_t⁻¹ (K)`. -/
theorem IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.symm (hΦ : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ) :
    Φ.symm.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF, K, hK, hFK⟩ := hΦ
  refine ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_symm_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hΦσ, _, hF.symm hΦσ,
    Φ.symm.cylinderMap '' (K ×ˢ univ),
    (hK.prod isCompact_univ).image Φ.symm.contMDiff_cylinderMap.continuous, fun p hp ↦ ?_⟩
  have hp₁ : p.1 ∉ K := fun h ↦ hp ⟨p, ⟨h, mem_univ _⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [hFK _ (by rwa [cylinderMap_apply, cylinderMap_apply, apply_mk_symm_apply]), neg_zero]

/-- The conjugate `f ∘ φ_t ∘ f⁻¹` of a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy `φ_t` by a
diffeomorphism `f` preserving `σ` is a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy. If the
Hamiltonian of `φ_t` vanishes off `K`, that of the conjugate vanishes off `f (K)`. -/
theorem IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph {f : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M}
    (hf : f ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (hΦ : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ) :
    (Φ.transDiffeomorph f).IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF, K, hK, hFK⟩ := hΦ
  refine ⟨SmoothForm.timeSlice_transDiffeomorph_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hf hΦσ,
    fun p ↦ F (f.symm p.1, p.2),
    HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph (F := F) f (by rwa [SmoothForm.mem_diffeomorphStabilizer.1 hf]),
    f '' K, hK.image f.continuous, fun p hp ↦ hFK _ fun h ↦ hp ?_⟩
  rw [cylinderMap_transDiffeomorph]
  exact ⟨_, h, rfl⟩

/-- On a compact manifold every Hamiltonian diffeotopy is compactly supported, with the compact
set `M`. -/
theorem isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_of_compactSpace [CompactSpace M]
    (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ) : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ := by
  obtain ⟨hΦσ, F, hF⟩ := isHamiltonian_iff.1 hΦ
  exact ⟨hΦσ, F, hF, univ, isCompact_univ, fun _ hp ↦ (hp (mem_univ _)).elim⟩

/-! ### The flow of a compactly supported Hamiltonian -/

section Flow

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [J.Boundaryless] [T2Space M]

/-- **The flow of a family of closed one-forms.** For a symplectic form `σ` and a smooth one-form
`Ω` on `[0, 1] × M` whose slices `Ω_t` are closed and vanish off a compact set `L`, there is a
diffeotopy `φ_t` whose velocity `X_t` satisfies `ι_{X_t} σ = Ω_t`, whose slices preserve `σ`,
and which fixes every point outside `L` at every time. Moreover `φ_t` moves the initial point of
every differentiable curve `γ` on `[0, 1]` with `γ' t = X_t (γ t)` along `γ`. -/
theorem exists_interior_velocity_eq (hσ : SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic σ)
    {Ω : SmoothForm ((𝓡∂ 1).prod J) (unitInterval × M) ℝ 1}
    (hΩ : ∀ t, mextDeriv
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val = 0)
    {L : Set M} (hL : IsCompact L)
    (hΩL : ∀ t, ∀ y ∉ L,
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val y = 0) :
    ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M,
      (∀ t, RoughForm.interior (Φ.velocity t) σ.val =
        (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val) ∧
      (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧
      (∀ t, ∀ y ∉ L, Φ (t, y) = y) ∧
      ∀ γ : unitInterval → M, MDifferentiable (𝓡∂ 1) J γ →
        (∀ t, mfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) J γ t 1 = Φ.velocity t (γ t)) → ∀ t, Φ (t, γ 0) = γ t := by
  -- The time extension `α` of `Ω`, and the constant family `σ'` of `σ` on `ℝ × M`.
  set α := SmoothForm.timeExtend Ω
  set σ' : SmoothTwoForm (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod J) (ℝ × M) :=
    SmoothForm.mpullback Prod.snd contMDiff_snd σ
  have hσ' (u : ℝ) : SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk u) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) σ' =
      σ :=
    SmoothForm.mpullback_prodMk_mpullback_snd u σ
  have hnd (u : ℝ) : SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk u) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) σ') :=
    (hσ' u).symm ▸ hσ.isNondegenerate
  -- The field `X_u = (σ♭)⁻¹ α_u`.
  set X : ℝ → (y : M) → TangentSpace J y := fun u ↦ hσ.isNondegenerate.interiorEquiv.symm
    (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk u) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) α) with hXdef
  have hX : ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod J) J.tangent ∞
      (fun p : ℝ × M ↦ (⟨p.2, X p.1 p.2⟩ : TangentBundle J M)) :=
    (SmoothTwoForm.contMDiff_interiorEquiv_symm_mpullback_prodMk σ' hnd α).congr fun p ↦ by
      simp only [hXdef, SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.interiorEquiv_symm_apply, hσ']
  -- On `[0, 1]`, `ι_{X_t} σ = Ω_t`.
  have hint (t : unitInterval) : RoughForm.interior (X t) σ.val =
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val := by
    rw [hXdef, SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.interior_interiorEquiv_symm,
      SmoothForm.mpullback_prodMk_timeExtend]
  -- `X` vanishes off `L`, so its suspension is complete.
  have hXL (u : ℝ) (y : M) (hy : y ∉ L) : X u y = 0 := by
    rw [hXdef, SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.interiorEquiv_symm_apply_eq_zero_iff,
      SmoothForm.mpullback_prodMk_timeExtend_eq_timeExtendSlice, SmoothForm.coe_timeExtendSlice]
    exact SymplecticGeometry.timeExtend_eq_zero (F := E [⋀^Fin 1]→L[ℝ] ℝ) (fun s ↦ hΩL s y hy) u
  have hc := isCompleteVectorField_timeDependentSuspensionField (hX.of_le (by simp)) hL hXL
  set Φ := timeDependentFlowDiffeotopy le_top hX hc
  have hvel (t : unitInterval) : ⇑(Φ.velocity t) = X t :=
    velocity_timeDependentFlowDiffeotopy hX hc t
  -- The slices of `Φ` preserve `σ`: `d (ι_{X_t} σ) = d Ω_t = 0` for `t ∈ [0, 1]`.
  have hpres : ∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ :=
    (forall_timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer_iff Φ hσ.isClosed).2 fun t ↦
      SmoothTwoForm.mem_symplecticVectorFields_iff.2 (by rw [hvel, hint]; exact hΩ t)
  exact ⟨Φ, fun t ↦ by rw [hvel, hint], hpres,
    fun t y hy ↦ timeDependentFlowDiffeotopy_apply_of_forall_eq_zero le_top hX hc
      (fun u ↦ hXL u y hy) t,
    fun γ hγ hγX t ↦ timeDependentFlowDiffeotopy_apply_eq_of_mfderiv_eq hX hc hγ
      (fun s ↦ (hγX s).trans (congrFun (hvel s) (γ s))) t⟩

/-- **The flow of a family of closed one-forms plus an exact family.** For a symplectic form `σ`,
a smooth one-form `β` on `[0, 1] × M` whose slices `β_t` are closed and vanish off a compact set
`L`, and a smooth function `G` on `M × [0, 1]` that vanishes at `(x, t)` whenever `x` lies outside
a compact set `C`, there is a diffeotopy `φ_t` whose velocity `X_t` satisfies
`ι_{X_t} σ = β_t + dG_t`, whose slices preserve `σ`, and which fixes every point outside `L ∪ C`
at every time. Moreover `φ_t` moves the initial point of every differentiable curve `γ` on
`[0, 1]` with `γ' t = X_t (γ t)` along `γ`. -/
theorem exists_interior_velocity_eq_add_mextDeriv (hσ : SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic σ)
    {β : SmoothForm ((𝓡∂ 1).prod J) (unitInterval × M) ℝ 1}
    (hβ : ∀ t, mextDeriv
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) β).val = 0)
    {L : Set M} (hL : IsCompact L)
    (hβL : ∀ t, ∀ y ∉ L,
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) β).val y = 0)
    {G : M × unitInterval → ℝ} (hG : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G) {C : Set M}
    (hC : IsCompact C) (hGC : ∀ p : M × unitInterval, p.1 ∉ C → G p = 0) :
    ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M,
      (∀ t, RoughForm.interior (Φ.velocity t) σ.val =
        (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) β).val +
          mextDeriv (RoughForm.ofFunction J fun y ↦ G (y, t))) ∧
      (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧
      (∀ t, ∀ y ∉ L ∪ C, Φ (t, y) = y) ∧
      ∀ γ : unitInterval → M, MDifferentiable (𝓡∂ 1) J γ →
        (∀ t, mfderiv (𝓡∂ 1) J γ t 1 = Φ.velocity t (γ t)) → ∀ t, Φ (t, γ 0) = γ t := by
  let Gc : C^∞⟮(𝓡∂ 1).prod J, unitInterval × M; 𝓘(ℝ, ℝ), ℝ⟯ :=
    ⟨fun q ↦ G (q.2, q.1), hG.comp (contMDiff_snd.prodMk contMDiff_fst)⟩
  set Ω := β + mextDerivₗ ((𝓡∂ 1).prod J) 0 (SmoothForm.ofFunction Gc)
  -- The slices of `Ω` are `β_t + dG_t`, and they are closed.
  have hΩ (t : unitInterval) :
      SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω =
        SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) β +
          mextDerivₗ J 0 (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id)
            (SmoothForm.ofFunction Gc)) := by
    rw [map_add, SmoothForm.mextDerivₗ_mpullback]
  have hΩval (t : unitInterval) :
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val =
        (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) β).val +
          mextDeriv (RoughForm.ofFunction J fun y ↦ G (y, t)) := by
    rw [hΩ, Submodule.coe_add, mextDerivₗ_apply,
      SmoothForm.coe_mpullback _ _ (SmoothForm.ofFunction Gc), SmoothForm.coe_ofFunction,
      mpullback_ofFunction, ContMDiffMap.coeFn_mk, Function.comp_def]
  have hΩd (t : unitInterval) :
      mextDeriv (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val
        = 0 := by
    rw [← mextDerivₗ_apply, hΩ, map_add, Submodule.coe_add, mextDerivₗ_apply, hβ t,
      ← LinearMap.comp_apply, mextDerivₗ_comp_mextDerivₗ]
    simp
  -- The slices of `Ω` vanish off `L ∪ C`.
  have hΩL (t : unitInterval) (y : M) (hy : y ∉ L ∪ C) :
      (SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t) (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) Ω).val y = 0 := by
    rw [mem_union, not_or] at hy
    have hGy : (fun z ↦ G (z, t)) =ᶠ[nhds y] fun _ ↦ 0 := by
      filter_upwards [hC.isClosed.isOpen_compl.mem_nhds hy.2] with z hz
      exact hGC (z, t) hz
    rw [hΩval, Pi.add_apply, hβL t y hy.1, zero_add]
    exact mextDeriv_ofFunction_apply_eq_zero_iff.2 (by
      rw [hGy.mfderiv_eq, mfderiv_const, ContinuousLinearMap.comp_zero])
  obtain ⟨Φ, hint, hpres, hfix, htraj⟩ := exists_interior_velocity_eq hσ hΩd (hL.union hC) hΩL
  exact ⟨Φ, fun t ↦ (hint t).trans (hΩval t), hpres, hfix, htraj⟩

/-- **The flow of a compactly supported Hamiltonian.** For a symplectic form `σ`, a smooth function
`G` on `M × [0, 1]` that vanishes at `(x, t)` whenever `x` lies outside a compact set `K`
generates a diffeotopy `φ_t`, which is a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy and fixes
every point outside `K` at every time. -/
theorem exists_isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian (hσ : SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic σ)
    {G : M × unitInterval → ℝ} (hG : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G) {K : Set M}
    (hK : IsCompact K) (hGK : ∀ p : M × unitInterval, p.1 ∉ K → G p = 0) :
    ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G ∧ Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ∧
      ∀ t, ∀ x ∉ K, Φ (t, x) = x := by
  have h0 (t : unitInterval) : SmoothForm.mpullback (Prod.mk t)
      (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id) (0 : SmoothForm ((𝓡∂ 1).prod J) (unitInterval × M) ℝ 1)
      = 0 := map_zero _
  obtain ⟨Φ, hint, hslice, hfix, -⟩ := exists_interior_velocity_eq_add_mextDeriv hσ (β := 0)
    (fun t ↦ by rw [h0, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, mextDeriv_zero]) isCompact_empty
    (fun t y _ ↦ by rw [h0, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply]) hG hK hGK
  -- `ι_{X_t} σ = dG_t` says that `X_t` is the Hamiltonian vector field of `G_t`.
  have hgen : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G := isGeneratedBy_iff.2 ⟨hG, fun t ↦
    SmoothTwoForm.isHamiltonianVectorField_iff_interior_eq.2 (by
      rw [hint t, h0, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, zero_add])⟩
  exact ⟨Φ, hgen, isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff_isGeneratedBy.2 ⟨hslice, G, hgen, K, hK,
    hGK⟩, fun t x hx ↦ hfix t x (by rwa [empty_union])⟩

end Flow

end Diffeotopy

namespace SmoothForm

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]
  [IsManifold J ∞ M] {σ : SmoothForm J M ℝ 2}

variable (σ) in
/-- The group `Ham_c(M, σ)` of **compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms** of a two-form
`σ`: the final diffeomorphisms `φ₁` of the compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopies `φ_t` of
`σ` (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian`). -/
def compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup : Subgroup (M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M) where
  carrier := {φ | ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ∧ Φ.final = φ}
  one_mem' := ⟨Diffeotopy.refl J ∞ M, Diffeotopy.isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_refl,
    Diffeotopy.final_refl⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro _ _ ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩ ⟨Ψ, hΨ, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨Ψ.trans Φ, hΨ.trans hΦ, by rw [Diffeotopy.final_trans, Diffeomorph.mul_def]⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro _ ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨Φ.symm, hΦ.symm, by rw [Diffeotopy.final_symm, Diffeomorph.inv_def]⟩

/-- A diffeomorphism lies in `Ham_c(M, σ)` exactly when it is the final diffeomorphism of a
compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy. -/
theorem mem_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup {φ : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M} :
    φ ∈ compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ ↔
      ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ∧ Φ.final = φ :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The final diffeomorphism of a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy lies in
`Ham_c(M, σ)`. -/
theorem final_mem_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup {Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M}
    (hΦ : Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ) :
    Φ.final ∈ compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ :=
  ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩

/-- Compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms are Hamiltonian: `Ham_c(M, σ) ≤ Ham(M, σ)`. -/
theorem compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_le_hamiltonianGroup :
    compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ ≤ hamiltonianGroup σ := by
  rintro _ ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩
  exact final_mem_hamiltonianGroup hΦ.isHamiltonian

/-- Conjugating a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphism by a diffeomorphism `f`
preserving `σ` gives a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeomorphism. -/
theorem mul_mul_inv_mem_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup {f φ : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M}
    (hf : f ∈ diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (hφ : φ ∈ compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ) :
    f * φ * f⁻¹ ∈ compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ := by
  obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩ := hφ
  exact ⟨Φ.transDiffeomorph f, hΦ.transDiffeomorph hf,
    Diffeotopy.final_transDiffeomorph_eq_mul_mul_inv Φ f⟩

/-- `Ham_c(M, σ)` is a normal subgroup of the group of diffeomorphisms preserving `σ`. -/
instance normal_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_subgroupOf_diffeomorphStabilizer :
    ((compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ).subgroupOf (diffeomorphStabilizer σ)).Normal :=
  (Subgroup.normal_subgroupOf_iff (compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_le_hamiltonianGroup.trans
    (hamiltonianGroup_le_isotopyStabilizer.trans isotopyStabilizer_le_diffeomorphStabilizer))).2
    fun _ _ hφ hf ↦ mul_mul_inv_mem_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup hf hφ

/-- On a compact manifold, every Hamiltonian diffeomorphism is compactly supported:
`Ham_c(M, σ) = Ham(M, σ)`. -/
theorem compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_eq_hamiltonianGroup [CompactSpace M] :
    compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ = hamiltonianGroup σ := by
  refine le_antisymm compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_le_hamiltonianGroup fun φ hφ ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, rfl⟩ := mem_hamiltonianGroup.1 hφ
  exact final_mem_compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup
    (Diffeotopy.isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_of_compactSpace hΦ)

end SmoothForm

/-! ### The milestone -/

namespace SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]
  [IsManifold J ∞ M] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [J.Boundaryless] [T2Space M]
  {σ : SmoothTwoForm J M}

/-- **Hamiltonian isotopies and their composition.** Let `σ` be a symplectic form on a
finite-dimensional Hausdorff manifold `M` without boundary, and write `X_t` for the velocity
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.velocity` of a diffeotopy `φ_t`.

* A diffeotopy `φ_t` all of whose slices preserve `σ` is Hamiltonian exactly when every
  `ι_{X_t} σ` is exact, and exactly when some smooth `H` on `M × [0, 1]` has `ι_{X_t} σ = dH_t`
  for every `t` (`H` generates `φ_t`, `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy`).
* Two functions generating the same diffeotopy differ, on each connected component of `M`, by a
  smooth function of time.
* If `F` generates `φ_t` and `G` generates `ψ_t`, and the slices of `φ_t` preserve `σ`, then
  `F_t + G_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` generates `φ_t ∘ ψ_t` (`Ψ.trans Φ`) and `-F_t ∘ φ_t` generates `φ_t⁻¹`; for
  `χ` preserving `σ`, `F_t ∘ χ` generates `χ⁻¹ ∘ φ_t ∘ χ` (`Φ.transDiffeomorph χ.symm`).
* The group `Ham(M, σ)` of final maps of Hamiltonian diffeotopies lies in the group
  `Symp(M, σ)` of diffeomorphisms preserving `σ`, and is normal there.
* A diffeotopy is a compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopy exactly when its slices preserve
  `σ` and it is generated by a function that vanishes off a compact subset of `M` at every time.
  Every smooth function on `M × [0, 1]` that vanishes off a compact set `K` generates such a
  diffeotopy, which fixes every point outside `K`.
* The group `Ham_c(M, σ)` of final maps of compactly supported Hamiltonian diffeotopies lies in
  `Ham(M, σ)`, is normal in `Symp(M, σ)`, and equals `Ham(M, σ)` when `M` is compact.

Milestone: *Hamiltonian isotopies and their composition*. -/
theorem isHamiltonian_iff_and_normal_hamiltonianGroup (hσ : σ.IsSymplectic) :
    (∀ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) →
      (Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ↔ ∀ t, σ.interiorₗ (Φ.velocity t) ∈ exactForms J M 1) ∧
        (Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ↔ ∃ G, Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G)) ∧
    (∀ (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) (F G : M × unitInterval → ℝ), Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F →
      Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G → ∃ c : ConnectedComponents M → unitInterval → ℝ,
        (∀ i, ContMDiff (𝓡∂ 1) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ (c i)) ∧
          ∀ p, F p - G p = c (ConnectedComponents.mk p.1) p.2) ∧
    (∀ (Φ Ψ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) (F G : M × unitInterval → ℝ), Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F →
      Ψ.IsGeneratedBy σ G → (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) →
      (Ψ.trans Φ).IsGeneratedBy σ (fun p ↦ F p + G (Φ.symm (p.2, p.1), p.2))) ∧
    (∀ (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) (F : M × unitInterval → ℝ), Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F →
      (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) →
      Φ.symm.IsGeneratedBy σ (fun p ↦ -F (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2))) ∧
    (∀ (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) (F : M × unitInterval → ℝ) (χ : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M),
      χ ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ → Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F →
      (Φ.transDiffeomorph χ.symm).IsGeneratedBy σ (fun p ↦ F (χ p.1, p.2))) ∧
    SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup σ ≤ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ ∧
    ((SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup σ).subgroupOf (SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ)).Normal ∧
    (∀ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ↔
      (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧
        ∃ G, Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G ∧ ∃ K : Set M, IsCompact K ∧
          ∀ p : M × unitInterval, p.1 ∉ K → G p = 0) ∧
    (∀ (G : M × unitInterval → ℝ) (K : Set M), ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G →
      IsCompact K → (∀ p : M × unitInterval, p.1 ∉ K → G p = 0) →
      ∃ Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M, Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G ∧ Φ.IsCompactlySupportedHamiltonian σ ∧
        ∀ t, ∀ x ∉ K, Φ (t, x) = x) ∧
    SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ ≤ SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup σ ∧
    ((SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ).subgroupOf
      (SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ)).Normal ∧
    (CompactSpace M →
      SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup σ = SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup σ) :=
  ⟨fun _ hΦ ↦ ⟨Diffeotopy.isHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms hΦ,
      Diffeotopy.isHamiltonian_iff_exists_isGeneratedBy.trans (and_iff_right hΦ)⟩,
    fun _ _ _ hF hG ↦ hF.exists_sub_eq hG,
    fun _ _ _ _ hF hG hΦ ↦ hF.trans hG hΦ,
    fun _ _ hF hΦ ↦ hF.symm hΦ,
    fun _ _ _ hχ hF ↦ hF.transDiffeomorph hχ,
    SmoothForm.hamiltonianGroup_le_isotopyStabilizer.trans
      SmoothForm.isotopyStabilizer_le_diffeomorphStabilizer,
    inferInstance,
    fun _ ↦ Diffeotopy.isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian_iff_isGeneratedBy,
    fun _ _ hG hK hGK ↦ Diffeotopy.exists_isCompactlySupportedHamiltonian hσ hG hK hGK,
    SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_le_hamiltonianGroup,
    inferInstance,
    fun _ ↦ SmoothForm.compactlySupportedHamiltonianGroup_eq_hamiltonianGroup⟩

end SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic

end TauCeti

